description:
System One gives you fast, bounded judgments from Jev over evidence you already have. Use it when a small semantic decision would otherwise cost you reading or reasoning: check a claim against test output or logs (sysone_check), find which of your excerpts answers a question (sysone_find), choose from a shortlist (sysone_select), or ask several of your own questions about one evidence set (sysone_decide). Call the tool directly; no setup call is needed.
Do exact work in code instead: counting, arithmetic, dates, versions, permissions, string matching, logs with explicit PASS/FAIL markers and searching files. Do not call it for trivial choices or to confirm an answer you already reached from evidence you read: each call costs a round trip and re-typed evidence.
Results are probabilities, not verdicts. Low support and low contradiction means the evidence does not settle the question. A relative choice can be irrelevant: include none/unknown and check an independent applicability reading. Unknown confidence requires review in gated procedures. Fit thresholds on labeled development cases, freeze them before held-out evaluation, and report coverage, wrong accepted decisions and review rate; there is no universal calibrated cutoff. Validate returned IDs and quotes in code. You keep every action and the final explanation. Do not retry a failed or uncertain call unchanged.
Use sysone_decide for independent questions over one state. Use sysone_code when an earlier answer changes the next input; within that program, batch independent questions with jev.evaluate. Await every jev call. Prefer direct tools when no dependent step is needed.

Check a claim against evidence you already observed, such as test output, logs, a diff or a command result. Returns the probability that the evidence establishes the whole claim and, separately, that it contradicts part of it; with evidence IDs, which item contradicts it. Both low means the evidence does not settle the claim. Use code for exact comparisons such as counts, versions or dates.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__system_one__sysone_check(args: {
  // Optional: your exact model ID if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  callerModel?: string;
  // The statement to check, e.g. 'All tests pass on main'.
  claim: string;
  // The observed results: text, or 1–32 {id, text} items so the answer can name what contradicts the claim.
  evidence: string | Array<{
  // Your stable ID, such as a file path, line number or log record ID.
  id: string;
  text: string;
}>;
  // Optional: your reasoning effort if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  reasoningEffort?: "none" | "minimal" | "low" | "medium" | "high" | "xhigh" | "max" | "ultra" | "unknown";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

