Ask up to 8 of your own yes/no (boolean), choice or score questions about one evidence set in a single evaluation. Each question reads the evidence independently and cannot see the other questions or answers. Use it when check, find and select do not fit. Include a none or unknown option in choices, keep record IDs in the evidence, and do counting and arithmetic in code.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__system_one__sysone_decide(args: {
  // Optional: your exact model ID if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  callerModel?: string;
  questions: { [key: string]: { criteria: { [key: string]: string; }; instructions: string; type: "choice"; } | {
  // What yes and no mean. A boolean probability is P(true), not a separate confidence score.
  criteria?: { false: string; true: string; };
  instructions: string;
  type: "boolean";
} | { criteria: Array<string>; instructions: string; type: "score"; }; };
  // Optional: your reasoning effort if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  reasoningEffort?: "none" | "minimal" | "low" | "medium" | "high" | "xhigh" | "max" | "ultra" | "unknown";
  state: string | Array<unknown> | { [key: string]: unknown; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

