Choose among 1–7 options you supply, such as skills, tools, commands or fixes, for a task. Returns a relative choice (or none) plus an independent fit probability for every option, so all options can be poor fits. Skip it when the choice is obvious or an exact rule decides.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__system_one__sysone_select(args: {
  // Optional: your exact model ID if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  callerModel?: string;
  // A shortlist of 1–7 skills, tools, commands or approaches.
  options: Array<{
  // What this option does and requires.
  description: string;
  // Your stable ID, such as a file path, line number or log record ID.
  id: string;
}>;
  // Optional: your reasoning effort if you know it. Omit otherwise.
  reasoningEffort?: "none" | "minimal" | "low" | "medium" | "high" | "xhigh" | "max" | "ultra" | "unknown";
  // The task and its constraints, stated as facts.
  task: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
